{"agent":"architecture","findings":[{"id":"arch-001","file":"triggarr/clients/base.py","line":233,"title":"validate_connection now logs raw httpx exception, abandoning the codebase's established sanitized-exception pattern","category":"pattern-consistency","cwe":null,"severity":"medium","agent_confidence":82,"in_diff":true,"intent_doc_match":null,"problem":"The codebase reduces httpx exceptions to a short summary such as 'HTTP {status_code}' or the exception type name before logging. It does this in four places: triggarr/search/engine.py:30 `_sanitize_exc` (its docstring says raw str(exc) 'may contain internal paths, URLs, or API keys that bypass the loguru redacting sink'), triggarr/search/scheduler.py:406 (which routes httpx/pydantic errors through `_sanitize_exc` to 'strip request.url credentials'), triggarr/clients/base.py:71 (the retry-failure log in this same file) and triggarr/tracking.py:70. This diff swaps `status=exc.response.status_code` for `exc=exc`. Loguru formats that with str(HTTPStatusError), which includes the full request URL (base_url plus path and query) and an MDN link.","current_code":"logger.warning(
